WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.840
Before Yona crossed the sea,
she already had stories to tell.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.820
“I was born in Sana’a.”

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.820
In Sana’a, her mother Margalit made clay
ovens. Yona’s small hands helped at home, too.

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.930
She was about nine when the family set out from Sana’a.

5
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.600
At the end of the long road lay a port.
Boarding a ship would have to wait.

6
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.890
In Aden, the family lived in tents.
The wait was measured in years.

7
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.210
“Four. I was there four years. My mother, five.”

8
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.950
A nine-year-old girl at the house
where Yona worked had a proposition.

9
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.510
“If you tell me a story, I’ll help you.”

10
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.920
And so Yona gained a pair of helping
hands, and the girl another story.

11
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.980
Thirteen and a half, Yona recalled. Heels
helped her look older for the doctor.

12
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.940
The permit was granted in Aden.

13
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.400
“The money we earned in Aden was
enough for my brother and me.”

14
00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:01.100
December 1934. After all that
waiting, hope had a date on paper.

15
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:11.640
Yona climbs the gangway. This
time, the harbor falls behind her.

16
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:18.380
The ship heads north. Between Aden and
Egypt lies the length of the Red Sea.

17
00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:23.830
In Port Said another change awaits the passengers.

18
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.200
“They moved us to another ship.”

19
00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.000
From there they set a course for Jaffa.

20
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.270
“But we couldn’t get into Jaffa.”

21
00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.890
Waves rose off Jaffa. A small
boat trying to land might capsize.

22
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.900
Jaffa was so close. Still, they turned north.

23
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.390
“They took us back to Haifa.”

24
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.380
At Haifa, Yona stepped onto
the quay and continued by bus.

25
00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.880
In Tel Aviv her destination was the
immigrants’ hostel on HaAliyah Street.

26
00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:06.800
Here she is in a photograph on Rothschild Boulevard.
Yona is on the right, beside her brother Yehuda.

27
00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:12.820
Yona married Shlomo in 1938. This family
photograph was taken four years later.
